Phasmid: Accept-Language, navigator.languages and the Intl locale

What:     Accept-Language is built from locale.languages exactly as stock
          builds it from the intl.accept_languages pref; navigator.languages
          is that list; the default Intl locale is locale.intl_locale.
Why:      The host's language settings show in the header and every JS
          context and must match the claimed locale.
Profile:  locale.languages, locale.intl_locale
Hooks:    chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc
          ProfileNetworkContextService::ComputeAcceptLanguage;
          chrome/browser/renderer_preferences_util.cc UpdateFromSystemSettings;
          chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
          ChromeContentBrowserClient::GetAcceptLangs;
          chrome/browser/preloading/prefetch/prefetch_service/
          chrome_prefetch_service_delegate.cc
          ChromePrefetchServiceDelegate::GetAcceptLanguageHeader;
          content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
          AppendRendererCommandLine, SetRunRendererInProcess;
          content/renderer/renderer_main.cc RendererMain; BUILD.gn deps
Contexts: main, iframe, worker, shared worker, service worker, headers
Guard:    tests/guards/locale/accept-language.py

